  "body": "Sensational location to the Waterfront, Village and Ferry Terminal - Genuinely motivated vendor after 18 years ownership.\r\nVacant, renovated, open plan, sun drenched 30m2 rear covered deck plus flexible settlement options. \r\nWith the extensive renovations listed below completed approximately 2 years ago, the lowest CV of $2,175,000 in the street and an asking price of $2,050,000, this is an opportunity not to be missed! \r\n\r\n•Full exterior and interior painting\r\n•New kitchen cabinetry, double sink and engineered stone bench tops\r\n•New carpet, curtains and Roman blinds\r\n•Main bathroom and ensuite updated including a bath\r\n•Electric RCD switchboard and LED downlights\r\n•Heat pump plus a gas fire serve the large open plan area\r\n•New clear roof installed over the deck a few weeks ago \r\n•Carport roof was just replaced, and the colour steel house roof was new in 2009\r\n\r\nHuia Street, named after the “sacred and rare” Huia bird, epitomizes the high rewards on offer to secure a foothold in this prime location, just meters to Queens Parade waterfront.\r\n\r\nOriginally built in the 1910’s, extended over the years (CCC’s all issued) plus the significant renovations as above, this exceptionally well-maintained Devonport property is ready for it's new owner.\r\n\r\nSingle level living with master bathroom & ensuite, perfect for young families or downsizers. Equally, if you are looking to invest and purchase with all the hard work done, this lovely home was previously rented for $1,250 per week.\r\nOutside the attractive gardens are low maintenance, included is a carport and at the rear a small shed, plus (keep secret) a large deliciously fleshed old fashion peach tree awaits your sampling this Summer!\r\n\r\nOptions abound from enjoying a morning coffee bathed in sunshine on the front deck, perhaps a walk up to the café and dairy at the top of the road, or almost certainly a leisurely evening stroll along the Queens Parade waterfront soaking up the sunsets and harbour activity on the way to your favourite Village café or restaurant.\r\nOpen homes are Sat & Sun 1pm - 1.45pm, or contact Peter Restall 021 808 808 for a private viewing.",
